  "notes": "SK-01 committed baseline. Captured via read-only kiln_call(name=\"get_stack_margin\") on 2026-09-24 while a heat/profile firing was active on the board (bench board memory: ESP firmware 75a5e459, per project memory project_bench_board_firmware_state; not independently re-queried here since board access was restricted to get_stack_margin and get_heap_status). A firing-active capture is deliberately the more conservative baseline per stack_margin_baseline.py's module docstring (mid_firing exercises profile_executor's tick path, relay/firing_stats writes, and the safety-link watchdog path that an idle capture never reaches). get_heap_status at capture time reported reset_reason=software (esp_restart), uptime_s=4138 -- consistent with the board having been up and running the observed firing continuously; it does not itself report an fw build/commit field, so the 75a5e459 commit above is carried from project memory rather than re-verified live. Two tasks read CRITICAL under this load: profile_executor (612 B / 4096 B, 14.9% headroom) and touch_uart_bridge (440 B / 3072 B, 14.3% headroom) -- both recorded as-is; SK-01 compares a live reading against whatever is committed here, it does not gate on this file being clean."
